WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.100
Looking closely at the formula, you might notice something surprising.

00:04.980 --> 00:07.960
It depends on the width W of the parked car in front,

00:08.380 --> 00:11.220
but it does not include the width of your own car at all.

00:11.760 --> 00:12.020
Why?

00:12.660 --> 00:15.540
Because in a single-suite maneuver on a wide road,

00:15.820 --> 00:20.360
the critical pinch point is your curbside front corner, a clearing point G.

00:20.860 --> 00:25.120
Making your car wider pushes edge BC closer to the center X,

00:25.460 --> 00:27.360
without changing the path of corner A.

00:27.360 --> 00:31.980
In real life, of course, a wider car does make a difference on narrow roads,

00:32.300 --> 00:34.080
or when you have to shuffle back and forth.

